; coverage test for automatic chain transitivity: declaring `chain OP1 OP2 ...` now generates
; a real, directly-usable transitivity axiom for every ordered pair of the chain's operators
; (`generate_chain_transitivity` in kurt.py), not just parsing sugar for writing one
; continuation-line chain expression. `arith.kurt`'s `chain = <= <` used to need 8 separate
; hand-written transitivity lemmas ("lt-trans", "le-lt-trans", ...) -- they're gone now,
; generated automatically from the `chain` declaration alone.
;
; this is a single derivation *step* citing the auto-generated fact directly -- unlike the
; older manual style (see proofs/arithmetic/order-transitivity-chain.kurt), no explicit
; `and`-combining step is needed to get from two separate facts to their combined conclusion.
load arith
var a, b, c

use a < b
use b <= c
a < c
;;; Proof checked.
